  "summary": "New models attach MD, energy and 3D-geometry heads to protein, RNA and ligand language models, turning embeddings into mutation- and site-resolved predictors.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is grafting physical supervision onto sequence foundation models. DynamicsPLM enriches a 35M-parameter PLM with residue-level and pairwise molecular-dynamics heads for zero-shot variant effects; MutAtlas assembles a PDB-wide atlas of exhaustive single-site mutations scored jointly by energy, language-model and inverse-folding terms; ProTEUS pretrains a mutation-resolved world model on deep mutational scanning coupled to a fast physics-constrained all-atom predictor for closed-loop evolution. The same fusion recurs for interaction sites: RSMBind pairs RNA language-model embeddings with 3D geometric descriptors, HieraPTM combines sequence, PLM and structure features with protein mechanics for functional phosphosite prediction, AllositeUltra learns cross-state apo/bound representations for allosteric sites, and HandShake adds cross-chain attention and contact supervision to ProstT5 for partner-specific interfaces. What is new is the move from embeddings-as-features toward explicit energetic, dynamical and state-resolved labels, plus actionable layers: PAMP projects a differentiable turnover objective onto discrete substitutions, and DecoyOpt uses ESM3-generated functional-site decoys for enzyme discrimination.",
